 "note": "Lunenburg High School. The page prints only 'FACULTY'; it follows directly on the Lunenburg High School report that ends page 47 ('Lunenburg High School would like to thank our community...'), and its departments and names match the 1999 high school roster. Lines 3-7 are ADMINISTRATION as label / name pairs (x 0.19 / 0.54), the label being the title in role_raw. Below that, two columns (x 0.12 / 0.54) of department headings governing the names under them, recorded in grade_or_dept. UNIFIED ARTS (line 16) is an umbrella over Computer Science, Business Technology, Industrial Technology, Band/Chorus and Art; HUMAN DEVELOPMENT AND PHYSICAL EDUCATION (lines 8-9) over Health/Human Development and Physical Education. Peter McCauliff is printed twice, under Computer Science (line 18) and Social Studies (line 29); both are recorded as printed. Honorific 'Mrs.' before Dawn Gearin is not carried in `name`. Line 52 is the page number."
